{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CfbhG2U8NiXUaqYtCBgib", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "The main difference is that **lists are mutable and tuples are immutable**.\n\n| | List | Tuple |\n|---|---|---|\n| Syntax | `[1, 2, 3]` | `(1, 2, 3)` or `1, 2, 3` |\n| Mutable? | Yes: you can append, remove and reassign items | No: fixed once created |\n| Hashable? | No, so it can't be a dict key or set member | Yes, if all its elements are hashable |\n| Methods | Many (`append`, `extend`, `insert`, `pop`, `remove`, `sort`, \u2026) | Only `count` and `index` |\n| Memory/speed | A bit larger, because it keeps spare room to grow | Smaller, and slightly faster to create |\n| Typical use | A collection of similar items whose size changes | A fixed record, where each position means something |\n\n```python\nnums = [1, 2, 3]\nnums.append(4)        # fine\nnums[0] = 99          # fine\n\npoint = (3, 4)\npoint[0] = 5          # TypeError: 'tuple' object does not support item assignment\n\nlocations = {(40.7, -74.0): \"NYC\"}   # tuple as dict key: OK\nlocations = {[40.7, -74.0]: \"NYC\"}   # TypeError: unhashable type: 'list'\n```\n\n**Gotchas:**\n- **A tuple with one item needs a trailing comma.** `(5)` is just the integer `5`, while `(5,)` is a tuple.\n- **Immutability is shallow.** A tuple can hold mutable objects. In `t = ([1], 2)`, `t[0].append(3)` works, but then `t` is no longer hashable.\n- **\"Changing\" a tuple creates a new one.** `t += (4,)` builds a new tuple and binds it to `t`. The original tuple is untouched.\n\n**Rule of thumb:** Use a list for a group of similar things that may grow or change, like a list of users. Use a tuple for a fixed group of values that belong together, like `(x, y)` or `(name, age)`. Tuples are also what you get from multiple return values and unpacking: `return a, b`. If you want fields with names, look at `collections.namedtuple` or `typing.NamedTuple`."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 7214, "cache_read_input_tokens": 16780, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 7214}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "not_available"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "9665c318-24c0-452d-b575-95471d43c3aa", "uuid": "bc49b51b-821b-4764-9143-fd661b0e980a", "timestamp": "2026-10-01T14:43:41.126Z", "request_id": "req_011CfbhG28oMAdvm4F2yY32P"}
